    "turn_text": "By the way, the Senate will take a procedural vote tonight on Murkowski's energy bill, setting up debate on the floor this week. Also, yesterday, the organizers of one of the largest energy conferences in the world announced that they're pulling the plug on this year's event, citing fears over the coronavirus outbreak. In a statement, IHS Market, which organizes the event, said they're canceling the Sarah Week conference because of the virus's quick spread. Sarah Week was supposed to begin a week from today in Houston, and usually it features the bosses of some of the world's biggest oil and gas companies and energy ministers from around the world. Over the weekend, the first death of coronavirus in the United States was reported in Washington State, and the virus has already turned up in 60 different parts of the world, while a cure still doesn't appear in sight. Subscribe to the Morning Energy newsletter at politico.com slash morning energy and subscribe to this podcast for free on your favorite podcast player. You can listen to this show on your smart speaker. Just search for the Politico energy podcast. Thanks and we'll be back again tomorrow.",
